From 482537cca61c2ce100452f7e2f187275a90e2e22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: matos <matos@local>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:24:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(polar): grouped FP64 path-GEMM UVU forward/reverse

Replace the per-node/per-path polar UVU kernels with 20 grouped FP64
path GEMMs (6 UVU tables: two field-dependent-charge blocks with dot/tp
plus LE q/v), a fused Hadamard/mask epilogue, a reusable saved-Z cache,
and the two adjoint passes reformulated as the same GEMMs.  Legacy
kernels remain selectable with MATOS_POLAR_UVU_GEMM=0.

1,296 canonical interleaved A/B: 255.35 -> 189.30 ms (-25.9%).
5,184 smoke: 988.28 -> 730.04 ms.  Parity 128/1,296: dPE=0,
max dF <= 5.8e-13.
---
